# Canonical repository instructions

Before doing any work in this repository, read the repository-root `AGENTS.md`
in full and follow it as the authoritative project rule set.

- `AGENTS.md` is the single source of truth for what BeaconMind is, the
  public-repo boundary, hardware and secret rules, where the project runs, and
  the Pico firmware port. `CLAUDE.md` points to the same file, so Claude Code,
  Cursor, and Codex all follow one rule set.
- If another instruction file or stale session context conflicts with `AGENTS.md`,
  follow `AGENTS.md` unless a higher-priority instruction or the user's current
  request explicitly overrides it.
- Re-read `AGENTS.md` after it changes during a task.
- Keep detailed guidance in `AGENTS.md`; do not duplicate excerpts into Cursor
  rules, because duplicated instructions drift out of sync.
